# NIC-Strelka — Povodok's own configuration options, beside Zephyr's
mainmenu "NIC-Strelka Povodok"

config STRELKA_FACTORY_PASSWORD
	string "the lock's password at the factory settings"
	default "strelka1"
	help
	  The application's password, eight characters at least (COMMANDS.md, The lock), as a
	  unit has it from the factory and after the factory settings, until the application
	  changes it by 64/17. The build's own choice; the firmware's default is provisional.

config STRELKA_CELL_EMPTY_MV
	int "The cell's end voltage, mV"
	default 3300
	help
	  Under it for ten seconds running, the unit goes off: a Li-ion or Li-poly cell at 3,30 V
	  until Povodok's cell is chosen. The fuel gauge's 0 % is not trusted until the cell's own
	  model is made (FIRMWARE.md, The PMIC).

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
